               Minutes of the Senate Committee on Computing Meeting
                                   16 April 1993

4.    CODE OF ETHICS

      ... the Dean [of Students] mentioned that the ethics
      document was too rough for him to comment in detail;
      however he thought the following statements should be included:

      1.    Before granting authorization (password, account
            no., etc.) to use McGill Computing Facilities,
            officials of the University who are in a "need to
            know" role to protect the security of the system
            or the security of other users' accounts should
***         have a statement waiving any privilege of
            confidentiality over any matter entered into the
            system.


